<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63895" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λοπ-ός</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόπος</span></b> , ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέπω</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>peel</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρομύοιο λ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					19.233
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of a hide,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. δέρματος</span>
			<i>the outer part of a split piece of leather</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτὸ τὸ δέρμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Art.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>peeling of the skin</i> after illness, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				2.1.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
